# Feature structure & Query

## Layout

```
src/
  app/                         # Expo Router routes only (thin)
  features/
    <kebab-name>/              # domain feature (e.g. rallies)
      screens/                 # feature screen bodies (+ screens/test/)
      components/              # feature-only UI (+ components/test/ when needed)
      hooks/                   # TanStack Query (and other feature hooks) (+ hooks/test/)
      db/                      # SQLite helpers only — no Query (+ db/test/)
      schemas/                 # Zod + inferred types (+ schemas/test/)
      constants/               # labels, placeholders
  shared/
    components/                # cross-feature UI (when needed)
    hooks/
    theme/
```

## Rules

- Domain code lives in `src/features/<kebab-name>/`
- Keep `src/app/` routes thin: read params, render the feature screen
- Cross-feature code lives in `src/shared/` (not top-level `components/` / `hooks/`)
- Cut the feature folders above even when they hold one file. Do **not** add `api/` `types/` `repository/` `docs/`, or barrel `index.ts` for integration
- Query lives in `hooks/`. `db/` talks to SQLite only. Screens import Query hooks, not `db/`
- Display strings live in `constants/`. Screens do not keep label maps
- Tests live in that layer’s `test/` (e.g. `hooks/test/`, `db/test/`). Do **not** colocate `*.test.ts(x)` next to the source file, and do **not** put a feature-root `test/`
- Do **not** introduce Repository interfaces, DI Context, or dual Memory/SQLite implementations “for testability.” Call SQLite (or a plain helper) from the feature; mock only out-of-process boundaries in tests

## Query = persisted state (local or remote)

SQLite, files, and HTTP are the same kind of state: they live outside the component tree. Use TanStack Query. `useState` / Context are for UI and session-only client state.

- `queryFn` / `mutationFn` may call SQLite or a plain feature helper directly (not only HTTP)
- Do not copy Query results into Context
- After a write, `invalidateQueries` (or `setQueryData`) so other screens stay in sync
- Local-only data mutated by this app: `staleTime: Infinity` plus invalidate on write is enough

```ts
// ✅ local DB is still Query
const { data } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ["stamps", "latest"],
  queryFn: () => getLatestStamp(),
  staleTime: Infinity,
});
```
